WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.918
Open WebUI can support reusable prompts, system prompts, task-specific assistants, conversation history, and workspace organization.

00:00:08.918 --> 00:00:14.053
These features help teams turn repeated work into more consistent workflows.

00:00:14.053 --> 00:00:21.619
A reusable prompt can standardize instructions for summarization, drafting, review, classification, or analysis.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:27.497
A task-specific assistant can combine a model choice, instructions, and expected style.

00:00:27.497 --> 00:00:31.754
Prompt templates should be clear, maintainable, and reviewable.

00:00:31.754 --> 00:00:38.104
They should explain the task, constraints, output expectations, and any source-handling rules.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:42.158
Vague prompts may work once but fail under different inputs.

00:00:42.158 --> 00:00:49.725
Prompts used by a team should be treated as operational artifacts that can be versioned, improved, and reviewed.

00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:55.940
Conversation history can improve continuity, but it can also mix contexts in confusing ways.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.345
A conversation about personal tasks should not become the basis for client work.

00:01:01.345 --> 00:01:05.939
Experimental prompts should not silently shape production workflows.

00:01:05.939 --> 00:01:15.060
Separating personal, client, experimental, and production workspaces reduces accidental data mixing and inappropriate reuse of context.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.357
Good workflow design is practical.

00:01:17.357 --> 00:01:28.032
Decide which prompts are reusable, which conversations are disposable, which files belong to which collections, and which model should be used for which task.

00:01:28.032 --> 00:01:32.356
The goal is to make AI assistance more reliable and less ad hoc.

00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:38.166
A well-organized workspace helps users understand what the assistant is doing and why.
